---
title: Configure a predefined/default filter in application
description: Create and configure default values for filter used in lists
keywords: 'ibm,carbon,maf,Maximo Application Framework Configuration,filter'
date: 11 July 2025
hiddenFromSearch: false
---

## About this task

Filter module uses QBE attributes to define its state. A QBE is an acronym for Query By Example and it can be declared as part of the datasource associated to the list. In the following example, it sets "CM" as initial filter for work type.

## Procedure 

### Step 1: Include a new tag structure of "qbe" and "qbe-field" to define query in the app.xml.

```xml
  <maximo-datasource-override id="todaywoassignedDS" […]>
    <qbe id="listQbe">
      <qbe-field name="worktype" operator="in" value="['CM']" id="fieldlistQbe"/>
    </qbe>
  </maximo-datasource-override>
```
> QBE accommodates EXACT and WILDCARD type of searchs.

### Step 1(alt): Alternative to declarative approach, one could also set QBE definition during datasource initialization.

```js
  // Custom Application Logic
  class AppCustomizations {
    applicationInitialized(app){
        this.app = app;
    }

    onDatasourceInitialized(datasource) {
        if (datasource.name === 'todaywoassignedDS') {
            datasource.setQBE('worktype','in',['CM','EM']);
        }
    }
  }
  export default AppCustomizations;
```

